# gitleaks baseline for history scans (make security-scan, CI secret-scan).
#
# Each line is the fingerprint (commit:file:rule:line) of a finding in a
# past commit, reviewed and classified below; gitleaks skips it, so a scan
# reports only new findings. Entries name a commit, so they never hide a
# finding in the working tree or in a later commit.
#
# Add an entry only for a reviewed non-secret in history that cannot be
# rewritten. A real secret is never baselined: rotate it first, then add
# it with a comment saying so. Rewritten history (rebase, squash) changes
# commit ids: rescan and review the reported findings again.

